{"name":"Hampton Beach","hex":"#9d603b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hampton Beach","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village and census-designated place in the town of Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hampton_Beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hampton Beach, New Hampshire","blocks":[{"text":"Hampton Beach is a village district, census-designated place, and beach resort in the town of Hampton, New Hampshire, United States, along the Atlantic Ocean. Its population at the 2020 census was 2,598. Hampton Beach is in Rockingham County, approximately 15 miles (24 km) south of Portsmouth. The community is a popular tourist destination and the busiest beach community in New Hampshire. Ocean Boulevard, the main street along the beach, includes a boardwalk, many shops and businesses, several seasonal hotels, and the Hampton Beach Casino Ballroom, which hosts national acts in the summer. Hampton Beach State Park was named one of four \"Superstar\" beaches in the United States in 2011, for having had perfect water-quality testing results in each of the previous three years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Hampton_Beach%2C_New_Hampshire.jpg/330px-Hampton_Beach%2C_New_Hampshire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hampton_Beach%2C_New_Hampshire","wikidata":"Q3472167"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/HamptonBeachNHMarch2019.jpg/500px-HamptonBeachNHMarch2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/HamptonBeachNHMarch2019.jpg/1280px-HamptonBeachNHMarch2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/HamptonBeachNHMarch2019.jpg/500px-HamptonBeachNHMarch2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ocean Boulevard in Hampton Beach, March 2019","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHamptonBeachNHMarch2019.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Hampton_Beach_NH_Sand_Sculpture.jpg/500px-Hampton_Beach_NH_Sand_Sculpture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Hampton_Beach_NH_Sand_Sculpture.jpg/1280px-Hampton_Beach_NH_Sand_Sculpture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Hampton_Beach_NH_Sand_Sculpture.jpg/500px-Hampton_Beach_NH_Sand_Sculpture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sand sculpture at the 2018 Hampton Beach Master Sand Sculpting Classic","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHampton_Beach_NH_Sand_Sculpture.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://